&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Place many named &lt;strong&gt;Excel Tables&lt;/strong&gt; on one worksheet&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bind each table to a JSON array and expand with &lt;code&gt;G=normal&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Know why tables use &lt;code&gt;G=normal&lt;/code&gt; (not &lt;code&gt;G=merge&lt;/code&gt;) and how &lt;code&gt;SUBTOTAL&lt;/code&gt; totals survive expansion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scale up from &lt;a href="../../m06-layout-style/m06-l01-table-style/"&gt;Table style retention&lt;/a&gt; to a real multi-table budget workbook&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;aside
 class="jx-lesson-demo my-8 rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50/80 p-5 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-900/60"
 data-jx-demo
 data-template-name="lesson_m09_monthly_budget"
 data-language="en-US"
 data-api-base="https://api.jsonxcel.com:2053"
 data-site-root="https://jsonxcel.github.io/learn-jsonxcel"
 data-sample-url="https://jsonxcel.github.io/learn-jsonxcel/samples/en-US/lesson_m09_monthly_budget.json"
 data-sample-kind="ds"
 data-template-url="https://jsonxcel.github.io/learn-jsonxcel/templates/en-US/lesson_m09_monthly_budget.xlsx"
 data-mode="ds"
&gt;
 &lt;div class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline justify-between gap-2"&gt;
 &lt;p class="text-sm font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-100"&gt;Interactive lesson demo&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Expense trend budget</title><link>https://jsonxcel.github.io/learn-jsonxcel/en/learn/m09-practical/m09-l07-expense-trend/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://jsonxcel.github.io/learn-jsonxcel/en/learn/m09-practical/m09-l07-expense-trend/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="learning-objectives"&gt;Learning objectives&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generate Jan–Dec sheets with a &lt;strong&gt;sheet template&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;code&gt;{{ds.items.month(S=None)}}&lt;/code&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build &lt;strong&gt;Summary&lt;/strong&gt; with &lt;code&gt;{{==SUMIF(...)(C=A5)}}&lt;/code&gt; — the &lt;code&gt;(C=A5)&lt;/code&gt; is required so every month column expands with categories (without it, Feb–Dec become &lt;code&gt;A5:A9&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;#SPILL!&lt;/code&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep a &lt;strong&gt;column chart&lt;/strong&gt; and &lt;strong&gt;sparklines&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;code&gt;{{(C=A5)}}&lt;/code&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep JSON flat: &lt;code&gt;items[]&lt;/code&gt; with a &lt;code&gt;month&lt;/code&gt; property&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Month sheets omit Excel Tables: table names must be unique workbook-wide, so sheet-template clones rename duplicates to &lt;code&gt;Table1&lt;/code&gt;/&lt;code&gt;Table2&lt;/code&gt;…. Use sheet-name SUMIF instead. (JSON &lt;code&gt;ds&lt;/code&gt; cannot use &lt;code&gt;F=&lt;/code&gt; filters today.)&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Blue sales report</title><link>https://jsonxcel.github.io/learn-jsonxcel/en/learn/m09-practical/m09-l08-blue-sales/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://jsonxcel.github.io/learn-jsonxcel/en/learn/m09-practical/m09-l08-blue-sales/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="learning-objectives"&gt;Learning objectives&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expand quarter headers &lt;strong&gt;horizontally&lt;/strong&gt; with &lt;code&gt;{{ds.季度名称(E=H)}}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expand product rows &lt;strong&gt;vertically&lt;/strong&gt; with &lt;code&gt;{{ds.rows.product(G=normal)}}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Spread each row’s &lt;code&gt;amounts&lt;/code&gt; with &lt;code&gt;{{ds.rows.amounts(E=H, C=B3, G=list)}}&lt;/code&gt; (&lt;code&gt;C=B3&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;G=list&lt;/code&gt; are both required)&lt;/li&gt;
